module v2.test.parse.supplied_token_stream_support

import v2.compiler.tokenize { tokenize }
import v2.extdeps.languages.dag { dag_lex }
import v2.std.compilers.lexing { Token, TokenStream, symbol_lexeme }
import v2.std.diagnostic { Accepted, Rejected }
import v2.std.logic { Bool }
import v2.std.text { String }

// SUPPLYING A TOKEN STREAM IS HOW A NORMALIZE-SUBJECT CLAIM PAYS FOR ITS INPUT ONCE. A claim whose
// subject is parse or normalize reaches its verdict through the whole text route -- tokenize,
// parse, normalize -- and that route costs more than the floor's per-claim budget before the
// claim asserts anything, so every such claim is refused on cost rather than on its verdict.
// DESIGN section 3 rules the remedy: supply the inputs at the boundary the claim discriminates at,
// and keep the real path executing somewhere. Supplying the TOKEN STREAM rather than the parse
// tree is what makes that practical AND keeps the subject whole -- parse and normalize both still
// execute on the supplied tokens, so a claim about parsing keeps its subject and needs no
// carve-out, while a token stream, unlike a production tree, is flat enough to author.
//
// THE PAIRING OBLIGATION IS DISCHARGED BY PROVEN EQUALITY, NOT BY ASSERTION. A supplied value is a
// hypothesis about a boundary; without a claim that the real producer emits that shape, the suite
// is green about a stream the compiler never produces. supplied_stream_matches_tokenize is that
// claim: it runs the REAL tokenizer over the same text and compares canonically, so deleting the
// integration reddens it. Each specimen owes one.
//
// SPECIMEN-SIZE CEILING, WHICH ADOPTERS MUST PRICE. This shape converts one over-budget claim into
// TWO claims that must each fit: the fidelity claim costs tokenize of its specimen, and the
// supplied-route claim costs parse plus normalize plus its assertions. That is comfortable for a
// small specimen and does NOT rescue a large one -- a specimen whose tokenize alone exceeds the
// budget hits the same wall through the mechanism meant to be the remedy, and must be split or
// dispositioned on its own. Measured 2026-09-22 on v2.test.parse.variant_field_lowering.
//
// The generator that authors a stream is deliberately NOT an authority here and is not shared: a
// second generator cannot produce a wrong green, because every stream is checked per specimen
// against the real tokenizer by the claim below. The generator is a convenience; this is the wall.
fn supplied_stream_projection(ts: TokenStream) -> String {
  fold(ts.all, init: "", f: fn(acc, t) {
    concat(concat(concat(acc, symbol_lexeme(sym: t.class)), "="), concat(t.lexeme, ";"))
  })
}

fn supplied_stream_matches_tokenize(text: String, file: Symbol, supplied: TokenStream) -> Bool {
  match tokenize(text: text, file: file, rules: dag_lex()) {
    Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => false
    Accepted { value: real, diagnostics: _ } =>
      supplied_stream_projection(ts: real) == supplied_stream_projection(ts: supplied)
  }
}
